~ start

if GameState.get_flag("met_zeus")
	=> shop
Zeus: So. A boy with a lyre climbs my mountain in the worst winter since the Titans.
Zeus: What do you offer a god for his attention?
- A song.
	Zeus: Ha! Songs don't buy bread. Though now and then they buy a god's curiosity.
- Nothing. I have nothing.
	Zeus: Then you're richer than most who climb these steps. They all come owing something.
- What would you take?
	Zeus: Olives, usually. My family are particular about payment. Remember that.
Zeus: Let's hear this lyre, then.
Orpheus: The strings froze on the way up. Two of them snapped.
Zeus: Give it here.
do World.restring_lyre()
Zeus: Gold thread, from my own cloak. Don't sell it.
Zeus: And a tune to go with it. My tune. Four notes: up, left, right, up.
Zeus: Some doors in this country were sealed by me, and they open for my song. There's one in the old temple, back west.
Zeus: Hold the lyre to play. It's written in your journal now. Everything worth knowing is.
Zeus: As for the winter: Hades called his wife home months early, and her mother has taken it badly. Seasons don't keep themselves.
Zeus: You want spring back? Go east, to Athens. My daughter likes clever things, and you seem almost clever.
Zeus: One more thing. A bronze bull has been grazing in the pen under the brook. Hephaestus swears it isn't one of his.
Zeus: It lets no one past. Hit it where the bronze is thin. Behind, boy. Always behind.
do GameState.set_flag("met_zeus")
=> END

~ shop

Zeus: Back again. Prayers, complaints, or business?
- Ambrosia, for thirty olives. [if not GameState.get_flag("bought_ambrosia")]
	if GameState.olives >= 30
		do World.buy_ambrosia(30)
		Zeus: Food of the gods. One more heart in you. Don't get used to it.
	else
		Zeus: Thirty olives. I can count, even if you can't.
- Remind me of your song.
	Zeus: Up, left, right, up. Hold the lyre and play it near a seal. Try not to embarrass me.
- Which way now?
	Zeus: East, through the bull. I did mention the bull.
- Nothing. Goodbye.
	Zeus: They all say goodbye. They all come back.
=> END
